IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Writ Petition (Civil) No. 13 of 2003
CITATION: (2013) 10 SCC 1
YEAR: 2013

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: P. Sathasivam, Ranjana P. Desai, Ranjan Gogoi

PARTIES:
PUCL vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Representation of the People Act, 1951, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 19(1)(a), Conduct of Election Rules 1961

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
nota option, right to reject, electoral democracy, voter secrecy

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Directed Election Commission to provide a 'None of the Above' (NOTA) button on electronic voting machines, empowering voters to express disapproval of all candidates.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 19(1)(a), Conduct of Election Rules 1961.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

